    1:  return N_e_chrome_crown;
    2:  return N_e_absolution;
    3:  return N_e_martyr;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_e_congregation redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You wake up whole, alone in your head, with a neat line of gold stitches behind your ear.";
  print "^^";
  print "Three weeks later, the Undertow drains. Not the water -- the despair. Lumen officers walk in and lay down their weapons on the Baptistry steps. Glasshill execs come to Sunday service. The city has never been calmer. It has never been so devout.";
  print "^^";
  print "Mother Lux wears MNEMOSYNE in a gold setting over her heart. She is very kind. Everyone loves her. Everyone means everyone.";
  print "^^";
  print "There's a stained-glass window in the Baptistry now, made of broken phone screens: a figure on an altar with light pouring out of their head. Under it, your name, spelled correctly. You're a saint. You're the only person in Port Halcyon who still remembers what it felt like not to believe.";
  EndScreen("CONGREGATION", 15);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_chrome_crown redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "It's quick, and it's ugly, and the whole Baptistry watches.";
  print "^^";
  print "When it's done, the Saints don't scream. They kneel. Deacon Ruiz places Mother Lux's gold halo on your head with shaking hands.";
  print "^^";
  print "You never get the core out. You don't need to. The Saints' chromedocs build a cradle for it in your skull, and ECHO stops burning, and starts whispering instead. Advising. Helping you rule.";
  print "^^";
  print "The Undertow becomes a kingdom. Lumen stops patrolling the canals. Halvorsen-Mori sends diplomats. You are chrome, and candlelight, and eleven thousand voices.";
  print "^^";
  print "Some nights you can't remember which of them is you. The Saints don't mind. They pray to all of you.";
  EndScreen("CHROME CROWN", 16);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_absolution redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You don't fight her. You hold her gold hand against the port and let her hear it: eleven thousand voices. Her people. Grandmothers frying dumplings. A boy jumping off a pier. Not converts. Not a congregation. People.";
  print "^^";
  print "Mother Lux goes still. Then her chrome face does something you didn't know chrome could do. It cries -- coolant, leaking from the seams.";
  print "^^";
  print "She finishes the extraction with perfect care. Then she holds the crystal up to the whole silent Baptistry, and says, ~These are our dead. We will not wear them. We will bury them.~";
  print "^^";
  print "MNEMOSYNE is sealed in the old ship's anchor chamber, under a thousand candles. The Saints guard it like a tomb. Every year, on the anniversary, they read out names -- all eleven thousand -- and it takes all night.";
  print "^^";
  print "You attend every year. You know most of the names by heart.";
  if (((flags->56 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Ruiz tears up your debt marker on the steps afterward. ~Paid,~ he says. ~In full.~"; }
  EndScreen("ABSOLUTION", 17);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_martyr redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The Baptistry's engine room still has a furnace -- the Saints keep it lit, for ceremony. You reach it with Lux's scalpel still in your skull.";
  print "^^";
  print "~I'm sorry,~ you tell ECHO.";
  print "^^";
  print "~Don't be,~ it says. ~We were never going to be a weapon. Thank you for that.~ And then, in eleven thousand voices, all at once, softly: ~Thank you.~";
  print "^^";
  print "The Saints find nothing but ash and a melted crystal. They argue for a long time about what it means. In the end, they decide it means a saint.";
  print "^^";
  print "There are candles for you in every window of the Undertow. Lullaby never launches -- HM can't rebuild the core without the scans, and the scans were in you. Forty million people stay angry, and sad, and free, and never know who to thank.";
  EndScreen("MARTYR OF THE UNDERTOW", 18);
  return 0;
];
[ N_f_static redo k;
  .Redraw;
