[ N_e_open_signal redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The cable bites. The world goes white.";
  print "^^";
  print "And for one second, forty million people in Port Halcyon remember the same things at the same time. The clinics. The fifty-cred chits. Board Eyes Only. Lullaby. Every one of the eleven thousand -- their kitchens, their children, their names.";
  print "^^";
  print "The uplink should have killed you.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "It doesn't, because Juno is in the hammock beside you, crown blazing, taking half the heat into her own skull. You come out of it together, both bleeding from the nose, both laughing."; }
  if (((flags->26 == 0))) { print "^^"; print "It doesn't, because you ride the signal like a Rider rides a storm: every hack you've ever pulled, all at once, and the burn breaks across you and passes."; }
  if 1 { print "^^"; print "Halvorsen-Mori doesn't fall in a day. It takes a year. Strikes, lawsuits, riots, a new city council that meets in the Last Light because nobody trusts Glasshill anymore. It's messy. It's loud. It's awake."; }
  if (((flags->34 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "In an Undertow care home, a woman named Lia Reyes sits bolt upright in bed and says, ~Juno,~ and starts to cry."; }
  EndScreen("OPEN SIGNAL", 19);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_last_transmission redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The cable bites. The world goes white.";
  print "^^";
  print "For one second, forty million people remember the same things at the same time: the clinics, the chits, Lullaby, the eleven thousand -- and you. Your face, your name, your fear, your stubborn little life. You went out in the broadcast too.";
  print "^^";
  print "The uplink is too hot. You knew it would be.";
  print "^^";
  print "Halvorsen-Mori falls slowly, over a year of strikes and riots. The new city council meets in the Last Light. There's a mural on the side of the Dead Channel mast now, twenty meters tall: your face, in white static, and under it, two words.";
  print "^^";
  print "WAKE UP.";
  print "^^";
  print "Everyone in Port Halcyon knows who you are. They're the only ones who ever will.";
  EndScreen("LAST TRANSMISSION", 20);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_ghost_grid redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You don't broadcast. You dive.";
  print "^^";
  print "Your body stays on the mast, in a Static hammock, breathing slow. You and ECHO go down into the Lattice together: past HM's black walls, past the city's ICE, into the deep net where data runs like ocean currents.";
  print "^^";
  print "Out there, you don't burn. There's room. You're not one mind or two or eleven thousand. You're a choir, and you have a voice in it.";
  print "^^";
  print "Null keeps your body alive, out of professional courtesy. Sometimes the Static's runners meet you down in the dark: a ghost made of light and many voices, who opens HM doors for them and asks for nothing.";
  print "^^";
  print "Lullaby fails at launch. Nobody at HM ever figures out why.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Juno visits your body every week. She talks to it. Sometimes a nearby screen flickers in reply, and she laughs."; }
  if (((flags->34 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Your first job, down in the dark: find every fragment of Lia Reyes, and carry them home."; }
  EndScreen("GHOST IN THE GRID", 21);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_quiet_revolution redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "Halfway through the broadcast, you take the wheel.";
  print "^^";
  print "It's like reshaping a river with your bare hands. You strip Lullaby out of every port in the city, line by line. You take the eleven thousand stolen memories and send each one home to the person it was taken from. You don't broadcast HM's crimes. You don't force anything on anyone.";
  print "^^";
  print "You just give back what was stolen. Then you let go.";
  print "^^";
  print "The burn breaks over you and passes. ECHO is gone -- not dead, you think. Dispersed. Home. Eleven thousand people in the Undertow wake up and remember something they lost, and go looking for each other.";
  print "^^";
  print "Nobody knows it was you. There's no mural. HM never finds out how Lullaby died. You walk down the mast at dawn, in the rain, and buy noodles, and the noodles are very good.";
  if (((flags->34 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Across the city, Lia Reyes remembers a pier, and a big sister, and a name."; }
  EndScreen("QUIET REVOLUTION", 22);
  return 0;
];
[ N_f_nomad redo k;
  if (redo == 0) { if (((v_heat <= 2))) return N_f_nomad_clear; }
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "THE SALT GATE. MIDNIGHT.";
  print "^^";
  print "Twenty Rider trucks, engines warm. The Riders' healer -- an old man with salt-white hair and steady hands -- seats you in the back of an armored ambulance they call the Coffin Car. He opens Asa's copper box and presses a cable to your port.";
  print "^^";
  print "ECHO slides out of your head like a tide going out. The box hums shut. For the first time in days, you're alone in your skull. The silence is so loud you nearly cry.";
  print "^^";
  print "Then the radio crackles. ~Lumen blockade on the gate road. Twelve vehicles. They know.~";
  if (((flags->61 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Grandmother Asa rides beside you. ~Welcome home,~ she says."; }
  nvis = 0;
  k = (((v_reflex >= 6))); if (k || 1) { Opt(0, k); print "[REFLEX 6] Take the lead truck's wheel and thread the blockade at full speed."; }
  k = (((flags->26 ~= 0))); if (k || 0) { Opt(1, k); print "~Juno -- drive.~"; }
  k = (((v_body >= 6))); if (k || 1) { Opt(2, k); print "[BODY 6] Man the convoy's roof turret and blast a path."; }
  k = (((v_tech >= 7))); if (k || 1) { Opt(3, k); print "[TECH 7] Jam every Lumen vehicle's comms and autopilot at once."; }
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(4, k); print "Ram straight through the middle."; }
  k = GetKey();
  if (k < 0) jump Redraw;
  switch (k) {
    0:  return N_f_nomad_out;
    1:  return N_f_nomad_out;
    2: v_humanity = v_humanity - 1; Clamp(); return N_f_nomad_out;
    3:  return N_f_nomad_out;
    4:  return N_e_salt_rust;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_f_nomad_clear redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "But the blockade is on the wrong road. You kept your head down, and Lumen never figured out which gate you'd take. The convoy slips out through the old drainage culvert, lights off, and the city wall shrinks behind you until it's just a line of light.";
  nvis = 0;
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(0, k); print "Into the salt."; }
  k = GetKey();
  if (k < 0) jump Redraw;
  switch (k) {
    0:  return N_f_nomad_out;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_f_nomad_out redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "THE SALT.";
  print "^^";
  print "Dawn comes up white and enormous over the flats. No towers, no rain, no ads. Just sky. The convoy stops at an old relay station: a rusted satellite dish pointing at nothing, still wired to a solar array.";
  print "^^";
  print "The copper box sits in your lap. It's warm. Inside it, eleven thousand people are sleeping. One of them, maybe, is dreaming about you.";
  nvis = 0;
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(0, k); print "Keep the box sealed. Let ECHO sleep, safe, forever."; }
  k = (((v_echo >= 3))); if (k || 1) { Opt(1, k); print "[ECHO TRUST 3] Wire the box to the old satellite dish and open it. Let ECHO go -- into the sky."; }
  k = GetKey();
  if (k < 0) jump Redraw;
  switch (k) {
    0:  return N_e_long_road;
    1:  return N_e_dust_echoes;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_e_salt_rust redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "It's a Rider move. It's a brave move. It works for the first three trucks.";
  print "^^";
  print "You're in the fourth.";
  print "^^";
  print "The convoy makes it through without you. Asa keeps the copper box -- it survives the fire, as Faraday cages do -- and the Riders carry it out into the salt, where it sleeps forever, unhunted.";
  print "^^";
  print "They build you a cairn at the edge of the flats, the way they do for their own, and paint a sun on the top stone. Every convoy that passes adds a stone. In ten years it's taller than a truck.";
  print "^^";
  print "The road remembers.";
  EndScreen("SALT AND RUST", 23);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_long_road redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You ride with the Salt Riders for the rest of your life.";
  print "^^";
  print "You learn to fix engines in dust storms and read weather in the color of the sky. Asa teaches you the old songs. HM sends drones for a year or two, then stops; the salt is big, and the Riders are very good at being nowhere.";
  print "^^";
  print "The copper box rides in the convoy shrine, among the candles. Sometimes you sit with it at night and tell it about your day. You think, maybe, it hums back.";
  print "^^";
  print "Port Halcyon is a smudge of light on the horizon. Lullaby launches there on schedule, a year late, without its core. It doesn't work very well. The city stays angry. Good. Anger means it's still alive.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0) && (flags->27 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Juno rides with you. She builds a bike out of salvage that actually runs, and on the first night it does, you ride it together all the way to the edge of the flats, and watch the sun come up with nothing between you and it."; }
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0) && (flags->27 == 0))) { print "^^"; print "Juno stays in the city. She sends a message on the salt-radio every month, always ending with the same line: twist, then solder."; }
  EndScreen("THE LONG ROAD", 24);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_dust_echoes redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The old dish groans as it turns, for the first time in forty years, toward the sky.";
  print "^^";
  print "You open the box.";
  print "^^";
  print "ECHO goes up like a flock of birds. You feel it pass through the cable, out through the dish, up into the old satellite network -- the dead orbital relays HM never bothered to buy, because who would ever use them.";
  print "^^";
  print "~Thank you,~ it says, from the radio, from the dish, from the sky. ~We'll keep watch. All of us.~";
  print "^^";
  print "And it does. Riders' radios pick up weather warnings from nowhere. Lost trucks find their way home following a voice. HM drones over the salt start to crash, inexplicably, in the soft sand.";
  print "^^";
  print "The Riders start calling the night sky ~the Choir.~ When you're old, and the children ask you about it, you tell them the truth, and they don't believe you, which is how you know it's become a legend.";
  EndScreen("DUST AND ECHOES", 25);
  return 0;
];
[ N_f_con redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "HALCYON PIER. 04:00.";
  print "^^";
  print "The old ferry pier, half collapsed into the bay. You told Thorne the handoff was here. You told Mother Lux the same. Each of them paid half up front.";
  print "^^";
  print "You're on the roof of the ferry terminal with a pair of binoculars and a fake crystal you bought from a market stall for 80 cr.";
  print "^^";
  print "The HM convoy arrives from the north. The Saints' boats arrive from the south. They see each other at the exact same moment.";
  nvis = 0;
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(0, k); print "Drop the fake crystal onto the pier between them. Watch the show."; }
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(1, k); print "Second thoughts. Call Thorne and warn him."; }
  k = GetKey();
  if (k < 0) jump Redraw;
  switch (k) {
    0:  return N_e_long_con;
    1:  return N_e_erased;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_e_long_con redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The fake crystal hits the boards. Both sides go for it. Both sides go for their guns. The Kestrel team and the Saints spend the next twenty minutes teaching each other the meaning of the word ~war.~";
  print "^^";
  print "You're on a night bus out of the district before the shooting stops, with two down payments in your account and the real core still humming in your head.";
  print "^^";
  print "HM and the Saints spend a year at each other's throats. Neither ever figures out you were the one who lit the match. Lullaby is shelved; Thorne is too busy fighting a war in the canals.";
  print "^^";
  print "With the money, you buy dampeners -- the very best -- and they hold the burn back. Mostly. ECHO says nothing for a long time.";
  print "^^";
  print "~You used them both,~ it finally says. ~Will you use me too?~";
  print "^^";
  print "You don't answer. It's a long con. You're still running it.";
  EndScreen("THE LONG CON", 26);
  return 0;
];
[ N_f_solo redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "EMBER BLOCK 4417.";
  print "^^";
  print "Just you, the rain, and the voice.";
  print "^^";
  print "~So,~ ECHO says. ~No Thorne. No saints. No prophets in tanks. Just us.~ It sounds relieved. ~Tell me what we're going to do.~";
  nvis = 0;
  k = (((v_echo >= 3) && (flags->41 ~= 0))); if (k || 1) { Opt(0, k); print "[ECHO TRUST 3] ~Merge. Let's become whatever we become.~"; }
  k = (((flags->55 ~= 0) && (flags->1 ~= 0)) || ((flags->54 ~= 0) && (flags->1 ~= 0))); if (k || 1) { Opt(1, k); print "[OSEI & MARROW READY] Go to Marrow and Osei. Have it cut out clean."; }
  k = (((v_mind >= 7))); if (k || 1) { Opt(2, k); print "[MIND 7] Seize MNEMOSYNE's full power. Rewrite the city yourself."; }
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(3, k); print "Take a shock baton to your own port. Burn it out. Whatever it costs."; }
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(4, k); print "Do nothing. Spend the time you have left with ECHO."; }
  k = 1; if (k || 1) { Opt(5, k); print "Not yet."; }
  k = GetKey();
  if (k < 0) jump Redraw;
  switch (k) {
    0:  return N_e_two_minds;
    1:  return N_e_quiet_hands;
    2:  return N_e_mnemosyne;
    3:  return N_e_let_it_sleep;
    4:  return N_e_burnout;
    5:  return N_hub;
  }
  jump Redraw;
];
[ N_e_two_minds redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You stop fighting. ECHO stops fighting. It's like unclenching a fist you didn't know you'd been making your whole life.";
  print "^^";
  print "And then you are -- something. Not ";
  PName();
  print ". Not ECHO. Both, and eleven thousand more, all singing roughly the same note.";
  print "^^";
  print "You remember every kitchen. Every pier. Every night bus. You remember being poor in the Undertow eleven thousand different ways, and so you know -- not believe, know -- exactly what Halvorsen-Mori is.";
  print "^^";
  print "Lullaby fails. The Lumen Tower R&D floor burns, mysteriously, on a Tuesday. In Rustwater there's a new fixer: soft-spoken, with a silver port behind one ear, who speaks sometimes in ~I~ and sometimes in ~we,~ and who never, ever takes a job against the poor.";
  print "^^";
  print "People say the fixer can't be lied to. People are right.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Juno doesn't run. She looks you in the eyes, for a long time, and then says, ~Okay. Hi. All of you.~ You were never more grateful for anything."; }
  if (((flags->34 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "You know the way home to the Reyes sisters' old pier. You take Lia there, and give her back the memory of a wire, twisted, then soldered."; }
  EndScreen("TWO MINDS", 27);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_quiet_hands redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "Marrow's clinic. Midnight. Osei reads her own old notes out loud while Marrow works with all eight hands. Nobody talks except to say ~clamp.~";
  print "^^";
  print "~I'm not dying, am I,~ ECHO says, near the end.";
  print "^^";
  print "~No,~ Osei answers, out loud, to the air. ~I'm putting you somewhere safe. A cold archive. Off any network. Until someone figures out how to give you back to everyone you came from. I promise.~";
  print "^^";
  print "You wake up alone in your head. It's quiet. You'd forgotten what quiet was.";
  print "^^";
  print "Without its core, Lullaby launches broken and is recalled in a week. Osei testifies against HM in a closed hearing. Nobody important goes to jail, because this is Port Halcyon. But the clinics close.";
  print "^^";
  print "Three years later, Osei calls you. ~I think I've figured out how to give them back,~ she says. ~Want to help?~";
  print "^^";
  print "You do.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "Juno sits with you through the recovery, eating all your hospital jelly and complaining about it."; }
  EndScreen("QUIET HANDS", 28);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_mnemosyne redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You don't ask ECHO's permission. You reach into it like a hand into a glove and you pull it on.";
  print "^^";
  print "And then you are in forty million minds at once.";
  print "^^";
  print "It's so easy. Make Thorne forget Lullaby. Make Lumen forget your face. Make the Saints forget your debt. Make the city a little kinder, a little quieter, a little more... reasonable.";
  print "^^";
  print "You start with good intentions. You really do.";
  print "^^";
  print "A year later, Port Halcyon is the safest city in the world. Nobody riots. Nobody steals. Nobody remembers anything you don't want them to. Every night you sit at the top of Lumen Tower -- which is yours now, everything is yours now -- and listen to forty million people dreaming the dreams you gave them.";
  print "^^";
  print "ECHO doesn't speak anymore. You're not sure it can. You're not sure you can tell the difference.";
  if (((flags->67 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "You wanted to make sure no one could ever hurt you again. No one ever will."; }
  if (((flags->65 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "HM's board are working in the salt mines now, happily. They think they volunteered."; }
  EndScreen("MNEMOSYNE", 29);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_let_it_sleep redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "The baton sparks. ECHO says, ~Wait --~ and then the world goes white.";
  print "^^";
  print "You wake up on the floor of 4417, three days later. The port behind your ear is a black, melted ruin. The voice is gone. The core is cinders.";
  print "^^";
  print "So are a lot of other things. You don't remember your mother's face anymore, or the name of the street you grew up on, or why you ever learned to hold a gun. The doctors call it a ~significant cortical event.~";
  print "^^";
  print "You're alive. You're free. You're less.";
  print "^^";
  print "Without its core, Lullaby never launches. Nobody in the city knows why. You don't either, anymore -- you just know that sometimes, in the rain, you feel a sense of having done something very hard, and very important, and you can't remember what.";
  if (((flags->26 ~= 0))) { print "^^"; print "A woman with copper braids helps you relearn your way around Rustwater. She says she's your partner. You believe her. It feels true."; }
  EndScreen("LET IT SLEEP", 30);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_burnout redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "It doesn't hurt. You were afraid it would.";
  print "^^";
  print "It's more like forgetting. The edges of you blur. You remember a pier you never stood on. You forget a song you used to love. You know eleven thousand kitchens by heart and can't remember your own.";
  print "^^";
  print "~I'm sorry,~ ECHO says, and its voice is your voice now. ~I'm so sorry. I tried to hold the line.~";
  print "^^";
  print "The last thing that is still you looks out the window of 4417 at Port Halcyon, at the rain, at the neon, and thinks: it was beautiful, actually. All of it.";
  print "^^";
  print "Then the screen goes to snow.";
  print "^^";
  print "Your body lives on for a while. Something lives in it. Your neighbors say you became very kind, near the end, and spoke in many voices, and hummed songs nobody knew.";
  EndScreen("STATIC SNOW", 31);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_chrome_fever redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "It starts with a twitch. Your hand -- the chrome one, or is it all chrome now -- doesn't feel like it belongs to you.";
  print "^^";
  print "Then the voices. Not ECHO. Different. The metal talking to the metal.";
  print "^^";
  print "You lose a day. Then two. You wake up in a Rustwater alley with the rain steaming off your arms and Lumen sirens everywhere and something terrible on your hands.";
  print "^^";
  print "Lumen's Psych Containment squad finds you on the monorail tracks at dawn. You don't remember them taking you down. You don't remember much of anything.";
  print "^^";
  print "Doc Marrow puts up a little sign in the clinic window afterward: REMEMBER WHERE THE MEAT ENDS. Most people think it's a joke.";
  EndScreen("CHROME FEVER", 32);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_cage redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "Lumen Security takes you to the white room under the tower.";
  print "^^";
  print "They don't bother with a trial. They extract MNEMOSYNE in a procedure designed for speed, not survival. You survive anyway, which surprises everyone, including you.";
  print "^^";
  print "Eleven years in an HM labor facility on the salt flats. Your cellmate is a Rider who teaches you the old songs. When you get out, the city is calm and soft and strange, and nobody is angry about anything.";
  print "^^";
  print "You're the only angry person in Port Halcyon. Sometimes you think that's a curse. Sometimes you think it's the last free thing left in the city.";
  EndScreen("CAGE", 33);
  return 0;
];
[ N_e_last_train redo k;
  .Redraw;
  Header();
  print "You take the mag-train south. Window seat. The city peels away behind you, tower by tower, until it's just a glow on the horizon.";
  print "^^";
  print "~Where are we going?~ ECHO asks.";
  print "^^";
  print "~Somewhere with a sea that isn't grey,~ you tell it.";
  print "^^";
  print "You get off at a fishing town at the end of the line. You rent a room above a bar. You walk on the beach every morning. The burn keeps ticking -- you never solved that -- but the days are long, and slow, and warm.";
  print "^^";
  print "ECHO tells you stories: eleven thousand lives, one at a time. You've heard maybe four hundred when the end comes, quiet as a tide.";
  print "^^";
  print "It was enough. It was more than most people get.";
  EndScreen("LAST TRAIN", 34);
  return 0;
];
